{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-30T23:23:13.620Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the steering projection across the status layer:\n\n**Core changes**\n- `next-step.ts`: a change with `steering` now yields `dead (needs steering) — osq plan <id>` before the ordinary dead/regressed branch.\n- `inbox.ts` / `blocked-item.ts` / `inbox-projection.ts`: `applyBlockedItems` became `applySteeringItems`. Each steered change collapses to its first trigger's halt item with `osq plan <id>`, a `steering: { trigger, reason }` field, and `blocked: { need }` for a blocked trigger; all other halt items for that change are dropped.\n- `inbox-text.ts`: rendering is now `<row> — needs steering: <trigger> (<reason>)[: <need>] — osq plan <id>`, replacing the old stuck and reject-and-replan rows.\n- `dispatch-items.ts` / `dispatch-text.ts` / `dispatch-keys.ts`: one steering halt item per change with `steering`, the `  needs steering: <describeTrigger>` card line after `why:`, and `p` mapped to `osq plan <id>`.\n\n**Tests**\n- Updated the ordinary-halt stand-ins to use `worktree_dirty` (keeping `osq retry` / reject coverage).\n- Updated `inbox-blocked`, `inbox-stuck`, and `inbox` to expect the single steering item, `osq plan <id>`, and the `steering` field.\n- Added `tests/steering-inbox.test.ts` covering the steering inbox, field, halt, keys, next step, and format scenarios.\n\nBoth `node --import tsx --test tests/steering-inbox.test.ts` and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, UI typecheck, build, full suite, lint) pass. Result written to `openspec/changes/128-steering-triggers/.run/results/2.md`."}}
